        "math_academy_id": "q-351007",
        "problem": "Express $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2x+1$ |  | $3x-4$ |  | $x-2$ |",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{A}{2x+1}+\\frac{B}{3x-4}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n18-19x=A(3x-4)(x-2)+B(2x+1)(x-2)+C(2x+1)(3x-4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =A(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(3(-\\frac{1}{2})-4) \\\\ \\frac{55}{2} & =\\frac{55}{4}A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{4}{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(\\frac{4}{3}) & =A(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(\\frac{4}{3}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(2(\\frac{4}{3})+1)(3(\\frac{4}{3})-4) \\\\ -\\frac{22}{3} & =-\\frac{22}{9}B \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18-19(2) & =A(3(2)-4)(2-2)+B(2(2)+1)(2-2)+C(2(2)+1)(3(2)-4) \\\\ -20 & =10C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{18-19x}{(2x+1)(3x-4)(x-2)}=\\frac{2}{2x+1}+\\frac{3}{3x-4}-\\frac{2}{x-2}.\n$$",
